  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - This consent is for a limited period of 9 months. This consent shall expire \r\non 19/02/2027 and the advertisement hereby approved shall be removed and the land reinstated to its former condition by that date.  \r\nReason: The advertisement is only acceptable for a limited period, having \r\nregard to the amenity of the area in accordance with  policy LP9 of the Local \r\nPlan and the requirements of paragraph 141 of the National Planning Policy \r\nFramework. \r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The maximum steady brightness of the lighting hereby permitted is not to exceed 300 candelas per sq.m.\r\nReason: To ensure the sign does not have an adverse effect on the amenity of the area in accordance with Council policy LP9 of the Local Plan and to comply with paragraph 141 of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Condition : 3 - The illumination of the sign(s) hereby permitted shall be by static illumination only. \r\nReason: In the interest of highway safety and of the visual amenities of the locality in accordance with Council policy LP9 of the Local Plan and to comply with paragraph 141 of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - INFORMATIVE: The applicant is advised of the need to apply for a scaffold licence in order to erect scaffolding on a public highway. Further information can be found here: https://www.wandsworth.gov.uk/business-and-licensing/licensing/highways-pavement-licences/apply-scaffold-licence/\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - INFORMATIVE: TfL have advised that all vehicles should only park/stop at permitted locations and within the time periods permitted by existing on-street restrictions\r\n"
  ],
